The level below was Demogorgon's, of course.  Demogorgon seems to be
much stronger in terms of damage dealt by hitting than in nethack,
which makes him more difficult, but he can (usually) be found in a
predetermined place, which makes him easier.

Here is my minispoiler for how to deal efficiently with Demogorgon in
slashem (effectively meaning that he is not likely to be able to make
you ill more than a single time).  Ingredients: an *uncursed* scroll
of earth, a cursed scroll of teleportation or a cursed potion of gain
level, an assault rifle or submachine gun, some 30 bullets enchanted
to at least (I believe) +4 (+5 is sufficient in any case), a wand of
secret door detection, a scroll of scare monster or a potion of
invulnerability, a potion of full healing (optional), water walking
boots or an amulet of flying (don't levitate by a ring), a digging
tool or a wand of digging, telepathy and a means of blinding yourself,
a scroll of magic mapping (optional), a potion of speed or the haste
self spell, if you don't fly, otherwise speed boots.  If you are a
hobbit, you also have the blink technique which allows you to be
superfast, not just very fast, for a few turn.  If you do it while
very fast, I think it means that you are guaranteed two moves in each
turn, three in some turns and sometimes even four, to obtain an
average of two and a half.

This is how to proceed: After going down the stairs, magic-map the
level.  This is useful to know at the turning of which corridor
exactly you will get in the line of sight of Demogorgon.  It is not
absolutely necessary, because proceeding carefully and using
telepathy, you will be able to determine that anyway, but it is much
more convenient via magic mapping.  Next dig out a space of two
squares around the staircase, as far as possible (it was at the upper
border of the map in my case so I could not get a stairs fully
surrounded by free squares).  If any spaces at a knight's move
distance of the stairs are blocked, leave them blocked, it is however
important to get as many free spaces at a distance of two squares in
the horizontal, vertical, and diagonal directions as possible.  Then
move onto the stairs and read an uncursed scroll of earth.  You will
be hit by a boulder, but that is no big deal with the AC you ought to
have (Luther wore a hard helmet).  [Alternatively, you might read a
blessed scroll and block the stairs with a scroll of scare monster and
an item on it - I did not try that approach, although I had two
scrolls of scare monster.]  Move one boulder to get away from the
stairs and move it back into its original position.  Then proceed to
the turning of the corridor, so that moving one step forward will get
you in Demogorgon's line of sight.  Detect any traps.  If there is a
fire trap just ahead of you, you should move diagonally into Demo's
sight or just dig out part of the wall until you find a place you can
step on without activating any fire or magic trap.  Take out the
scroll of scare monster or your potion of invulnerability and your
potion of full healing (if you want to rely on that for getting rid of
the illness).  Ready your rifle, quiver your bullets, quaff the potion
of invulnerability.  Since you should be very fast at least, you can
determine the appropriate time to move ahead so you have a second free
move in the turn (move after waiting gave you only one move in a
turn).  This is easier for hobbits.  They invoke their blink technique
and just move ahead, having two guaranteed moves anyway (if they
started very fast, that is).  Now you have one free move to shoot at
Demogorgon, or as it turned out in Luther's case, at the monster that
is in front of him.  This was some kind of devil who fell after the
fourth of the five +7 bullets that Luther sent, so only one bullet hit
Demogorgon.  Anyway, Luther got another round of shots, but apparently
Demogorgon had gone.  Here, I didn't work optimally, because Luther
wore the Eyes instead of the blindfold, so he could not see what
actually had happened.  For fear that Demo would turn up next to him
immediately, he dropped the scroll of scare monster, which actually
would have been unnecessary.  Donning the blindfold revealed that
being hit by one bullet had been sufficiently scary for Demo to
teleport near the stairs (not *on* them, there was a boulder
there...).  In general, either the potion of invulnerability or the
scroll of scare monster are intended to protect you, should you not do
enough damage on the first encounter for Demogorgon to teleport away -
he would in that case most likely teleport next to you.  (The potion
is preferable, in case Demo puts a pool below you via a spell, but I
did not have the potion).  If you manage to damage him enough in the
first round of shooting, he will however never come close to you; this
was the case with Luther who ended up following the miniconduct "you
never were ill".  As soon as Demogorgon is near the stairs, teleport
one level up or use the potion of gain level for the same end (Luther
teleported).  Then go down the stairs - "There is a boulder here".
Well, but that does not matter, since it does not impede your
movements.  Now wait until Demogorgon who cannot do anything to you,
is in a convenient position, two squares away horizontally,
vertically, or diagonally.  Shoot at him, repeat if necessary.  Two
rounds should be sufficient.  You cannot shoot at him when he is in a
knight's position, but he is very mobile, he cannot sit still, trying
to get to you in vain.  Luther needed two rounds to finish him off,
since Demo had been hit only by one bullet initially.  Total number of
bullets spent - slightly more than twenty.  After that, Luther was
happy and did not spend too much time thinking about how to beat the
other, lesser demon princes.  He removed or pick-axed the boulders
around the staircase and proceeded.  Unfortunately, he was hit by a
potion of amnesia on the same level and had to remap it (and a number
of other levels on the ascension run, he was also hit a second time by
a potion of amnesia).

